<title>UK: BA directors resign from USAir board.</title>
<headline>BA directors resign from USAir board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Tuesday three of its directors had resigned from the board of U.S. carrier USAir following BA's decision in December last year to cut its ties with USAir.</p>
<p>BA said Bob Ayling, chief executive, Derek Stevens, chief financial officer and Roger Maynard, director of investments and joint ventures, had resigned from the USAir board.</p>
<p>BA announced the planned resignations in December.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
